{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}

{% block content %}
<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pt-24 pb-8 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500">Private preview</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Free during preview. No surprise bill.</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-600">Forest pricing is still being validated with design partners. Billing is not active, there is no SLA, and preview users will not be charged without a separate agreement and advance notice.</p>
</section>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="p-8 border-2 border-gray-900 rounded-lg">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
                <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">Private Preview</h2>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500">Invite-only · $0 · No SLA</p>
            </div>
            <a href="mailto:contact@kjuulh.io?subject=Forest%20private%20preview" class="inline-flex px-4 py-2 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-md text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-800">
                Join waitlist
            </a>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
            <li>Private component exchange</li>
            <li>Typed project and CI dependencies</li>
            <li>Developer-tool catalogues</li>
            <li>Limits agreed during onboarding</li>
            <li>Community support</li>
            <li>Customer-run execution is unmetered</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center">How paid pricing is being designed</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="p-5 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold">Managed exchange</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Future pricing will cover the private registry, control plane, collaboration, policy, and support—not compute Forest does not provide.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold">Active developers</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">The leading seat metric counts a human once per active UTC month. Machine identities will not consume human seats.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold">Transparent usage</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Storage and artifact egress may have allowances. Usage export, budget alerts, and advance notice must exist before overage charging.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="p-6 border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-lg">Trusted components only</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">Forest is currently suitable only for trusted internal evaluation on a private network. Native components run with the invoking user's privileges, and runner/artifact authorization is not ready for mutually untrusted tenants. Sandboxed managed execution, workload identity, permanent coordinates, provenance, and artifact scanning are productization gates—not paid add-ons or shipped preview guarantees.</p>
    </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
